    "caveats": [
      "Verify antipyrine's low-extraction classification and target E against your own literature; E = 0.15 is a design target, not a measured value — measure C_out by LC-MS/MS to confirm.",
      "Run a cell-free (blank) PDMS chip control to subtract antipyrine binding to PDMS/tubing; antipyrine is lipophilic enough to adsorb.",
      "HepG2 is an immortalized hepatoma with reduced CYP activity vs primary hepatocytes — for true intrinsic metabolic capacity consider primary human hepatocytes (BSL-2) or HepaRG.",
      "Confirm the 0.05 Pa shear is acceptable; it is at the bottom of the HepG2 physiological range — if cells detach, raise flow (which raises E toward flow-limited, so re-check the low-extraction assumption).",
      "The 200 µL system volume and 24 h dose interval are assumptions for recirculating half-life/accumulation estimates — measure your actual reservoir + tubing volume.",
      "Antipyrine clearance is slow; ensure sampling times are long enough (hours) to resolve a 0.15 extraction from analytical noise."
    ]
  },
